# AUVRA database migrations

The active Alembic revision path is `recovery_versions/`. It starts with the
immutable `20260723_0001` canonical baseline for a completely blank PostgreSQL
17 database.

The files in `versions/` are historical evidence only. They are deliberately
not included in `version_locations`: replaying them is not a supported install
or recovery path. Never point the canonical baseline at an old populated
database and never stamp an old database as the canonical baseline.

For bootstrap, validation, and approved legacy-data migration instructions,
see `docs/DATABASE_RECOVERY.md`.
